      </operator>
      <connect from_port="input 1" to_op="Handle Exception" to_port="in 1"/>
      <connect from_op="Handle Exception" from_port="out 1" to_port="result 1"/>
      <portSpacing port="source_input 1" spacing="0"/>
      <portSpacing port="source_input 2" spacing="0"/>
      <portSpacing port="sink_result 1" spacing="0"/>
      <portSpacing port="sink_result 2" spacing="0"/>
      <description align="center" color="blue" colored="true" height="707" resized="true" width="183" x="724" y="2112">Preprocessing Stage&lt;br&gt;Calculating PTA tags, dol (if any), inferred tags, input data check</description>
      <description align="center" color="purple" colored="true" height="706" resized="true" width="208" x="1142" y="2180">Optimum Stage&lt;br&gt;Read/Pull Clean data, calculate respective inferred tags and Clean data processing</description>
      <description align="center" color="red" colored="true" height="708" resized="true" width="275" x="1423" y="2140">Postprocessing Stage&lt;br&gt;Finding best benchmarks, generate optimization tags (if any), preparing output into required format</description>
      <description align="center" color="orange" colored="true" height="708" resized="true" width="390" x="307" y="1978">Initialization Stage&lt;br&gt;Read tables, make pi and sql connections and generate LBM specific macros</description>
      <description align="center" color="blue" colored="true" height="701" resized="true" width="292" x="10" y="1888">LBM Pipeline&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Author&lt;br&gt;Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;Karthik Venkata&lt;br&gt;Nikhil Khandare&lt;br&gt;Sagar Warke&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Live Benchmarking Model is a dynamic and real-time process of comparing and evaluating the performance of the plant data against defined standards or established benchmarks. Unlike traditional benchmarking, which typically involves periodic assessments and comparisons, live benchmarking continuously monitors and analyzes performance metrics, allowing for immediate feedback and adjustments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="336" resized="false" width="126" x="337" y="2091">Can input manually like case id if wants to run process independently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: PI Server Connection&lt;br&gt;I/P 2: SQL Server Connection&lt;br&gt;I/P 3 : Table Names&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P 1: PI Server Connection&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: SQL Server Connection&lt;br&gt;O/P 3 : Table Names&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="282" resized="false" width="126" x="517" y="2222">Process Read all required tables and pull data from PI server according to date ranges given in case info.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: PI Server Connection&lt;br&gt;I/P 2: SQL Server Connection&lt;br&gt;I/P 3 : Table Names&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;O/P : Pi tags data</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="228" resized="false" width="126" x="751" y="2258">Process calculate inferred tags of all the categories, generate dol (if required) and do input data checks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: Pi tags data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P : Inferred tags along with pi tags data</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="228" resized="false" width="126" x="975" y="2294">Process calculate inferred tags of all the categories, generate dol (if required) and do input data checks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: Pi tags data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P : Inferred tags along with pi tags data</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="336" resized="false" width="126" x="1173" y="2313">Process mainly deals with clean data. Perform required operations like calculating inferred tags and applying limit filters,etc&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P : Current data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P 1: filtered clean data&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: Normalized model&lt;br&gt;O/P 3 : Current raw data</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="444" resized="false" width="126" x="1512" y="2242">Process perform Postprocessing steps on clean and current raw data like finding optimum records, creating optimization results, etc&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: filtered clean data&lt;br&gt;I/P 2: Normalized model&lt;br&gt;I/P 3 : Current raw data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P 1: LBM Model Status&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: LBM Output&lt;br&gt;O/P 3: LBM Skip Status Type&lt;br&gt;O/P 4: Model Output Trend</description>
      <description align="center" color="purple" colored="true" height="551" resized="true" width="226" x="18" y="16">What if optimizer&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Author:&lt;br&gt;Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;Karthik Sanagapalli&lt;br&gt;Sai Siva Pedapalem&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Overview:&lt;br&gt;This process uses the calculated demand&amp;#8212;derived from user-provided plant parameters&amp;#8212;along with inputs such as equipment availability and pricing. These combined inputs are then fed into the gekko optimizer, which runs to determine the best or most optimal solution based on the user's specified requirements.&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <description align="center" color="blue" colored="true" height="551" resized="true" width="317" x="251" y="16">Energy Optimization</description>
    </process>
  </operator>
</process>
